{"batchcomplete":"","query":{"normalized":[{"from":"True_Grit","to":"True Grit"},{"from":"Signature_Move","to":"Signature Move"},{"from":"Shrug_It_Off","to":"Shrug It Off"},{"from":"Blood_for_Blood","to":"Blood for Blood"},{"from":"Empty_Mind","to":"Empty Mind"},{"from":"Machine_Learning","to":"Machine Learning"},{"from":"All-Out_Attack","to":"All-Out Attack"},{"from":"Thunder_Strike","to":"Thunder Strike"},{"from":"Second_Wind","to":"Second Wind"},{"from":"Strike_(Silent)","to":"Strike (Silent)"},{"from":"Grand_Finale","to":"Grand Finale"},{"from":"Deadly_Poison","to":"Deadly Poison"},{"from":"Burning_Pact","to":"Burning Pact"}],"pages":{"1795":{"pageid":1795,"ns":0,"title":"All-Out Attack","revisions":[{"revid":56312,"parentid":55302,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = All-Out Attack\n| Image       = Green-All-OutAttack.png\n| Color       = Green\n| Type        = Attack\n| Rarity      = Uncommon\n| Cost        = 1\n| Description = Deal (10;14) damage to ALL enemies.<br>Discard 1 card at random.\n| GivesToPlayer = Discard\n}}\n{{C|All-Out Attack}} is a 1 {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 10 (14 if upgraded) damage to '''ALL''' enemies, and randomly [[Keywords#Discard|discards]] one card in your hand. If there are no other cards in hand when this card is played, no card will be [[Keywords#Discard|discarded]].\n\n== Interactions == \n=== Synergies ===\n* Although the random targeting makes this unreliable, {{C|All-Out Attack}}'s [[Keywords#Discard|discard]] effect synergises with several [[Silent]] cards and relics: \n\n==== Cards ====\n* [[Keywords#Discard|Discarding]] {{C|Tactician}} or {{C|Reflex}} will immediately activate their effects.\n* {{C|Eviscerate}} is discounted by 1 {{Icon|GE}} Energy this turn.\n* {{C|Sneaky Strike}} will now refund 2 {{Icon|GE}} Energy if also played this turn.\n\n==== Relics ====\n* {{R|Tough Bandages}} will grant 3 {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{R|Tingsha}} will deal 3 damage to a random enemy.\n* {{R|Hovering Kite}} will generate 1 {{Icon|GE}} Energy if this is the first time a card has been [[Keywords#Discard|discarded]] this turn.\n\n=== Neutral === \n* {{C|All-Out Attack}} can also be used to [[Keywords#Discard|discard]] cards with end-of-turn effects, like {{C|Burn}} or {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curses}} such as {{C|Regret}}.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* The card's artwork, a cloud with fists popping out suggesting rapid beatings, is a reference to the move of the same name from the Persona series.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V1.1: The Dealer'''\n** All-Out Attack, Madness, and Reboot cards no longer affect Card Rewards when used (rng issue).\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 45: Impatience'''\n** All Out Attack card's discards now utilize seeds.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 17: Patched in the Face'''\n** All Out Attack card rework + buff. Now discards 1 card at random rather than card draw reduction.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 5: Happy Holidays!'''\n** Bird-Faced, Well-Laid, All-Out, Self-Forming gets hyphenated.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 3: Balance Balance Balance'''\n** All Out Attack card's drawback now stacks in a more sensible manner.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1881":{"pageid":1881,"ns":0,"title":"Blood for Blood","revisions":[{"revid":56417,"parentid":55656,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Blood for Blood\n| Image       = Red-BloodforBlood.png\n| Color       = Red\n| Type        = Attack\n| Rarity      = Uncommon\n| Cost        = 4\n| CostPlus    = 3\n| Description = Costs 1 less {{Icon|RE}}<br>for each time you lose HP this combat.<br>Deal (18;22) damage.\n| InteractsWith = Lose HP\n}}\n{{C|Blood for Blood}} is a 4 (3 if upgraded) {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 18 (22 if upgraded) damage, and costs 1 less {{Icon|RE}} '''Energy''' for every time you have lost HP this combat, no matter the source or amount of this HP loss.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* Unlike most other cards with {{Icon|RE}} '''Energy'''-reducing upgrades that have had their cost randomized by {{BD|Confused}} or {{P|Snecko Oil}}, a {{C|Blood for Blood}} that costs more than 0 {{Icon|RE}} '''Energy''' will always go down by 1 in {{Icon|RE}}-cost when {{KW|Upgrade|Upgraded}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* When reducing the {{Icon|RE}}-cost of {{C|Blood for Blood}} through an effect such as {{P|Liquid Memories}} or {{C|Enlightenment}}, losing HP or upgrading {{C|Blood for Blood}} will continue to lower the cost as normal.\n** If the original {{Icon|RE}}-cost reduction was temporary, such as through an unupgraded {{C|Enlightenment}}, any cost reductions as a result of upgrading or losing HP will apply to the cost {{C|Blood for Blood}} had before this reduction once it wears off.\n\n* If this card is created during combat, such as through {{C|Metamorphosis}}, an {{P|Attack Potion}} or {{R|Dead Branch}}, it will account for HP lost before it existed. \n** This is unlike {{C|Masterful Stab}}, which will start at 0 {{Icon|GE}}-cost. \n\n== Trivia ==\n* '''Blood For Blood''' was briefly included in Slay the Spire 2's early development, before being removed in [[sts2:V0.40.0 - Pre-release Version|V0.40.0]] along with Entrench.<ref>https://youtu.be/ttVtllHkb4E&t=50</ref>\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 49: The Designer'''\n** Fixed cards like Blood for Blood and Masterful Stab being affected outside of combat.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 18: Paranormal'''\n** Blood for Blood card buff. 16 -> 18. Upgraded: 18 -> 22.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 8: Ooh Shiny!'''\n** Fixed issue where Blood for Blood cost was permanently lowered if damaged at Neow.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1882":{"pageid":1882,"ns":0,"title":"Burning Pact","revisions":[{"revid":56418,"parentid":50413,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Burning Pact\n| Image       = Red-BurningPact.png\n| Color       = Red\n| Type        = Skill\n| Rarity      = Uncommon\n| Cost        = 1\n| Description = {{KW|Exhaust}} 1 card.<br>Draw (2;3) cards.\n| GivesToPlayer = Exhaust, Draw\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Burning Pact}} is a 1 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It makes you select one card in hand to {{KW|Exhaust}} and draws 2 (3 if upgraded) cards.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* Selecting a card to {{KW|Exhaust}} happens ''before'' drawing, meaning a card that is already in hand when this card is played must be {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}}. If there are no other cards in hand when this card is played, no card will be {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}}.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* Has {{KW|Exhaust}}-synergy with {{C|Dark Embrace}}, {{C|Feel No Pain}}, {{R|Charon's Ashes}} and {{R|Dead Branch}}, and can reliably {{KW\n|Exhaust}} {{C|Sentinel}}.\n* {{C|Burning Pact}} can be used to get rid of unwanted cards in hand, such as {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Status|Status}} or {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}} cards.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2427":{"pageid":2427,"ns":0,"title":"Collect","revisions":[{"revid":56943,"parentid":55702,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Collect\n|Image       = Purple-Collect.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = -1\n|Description = Put a {{C|Miracle|Miracle+}} into your hand at the start of your next (X;X+1) turns. {{KW|Exhaust}}\n|GivesToPlayer = Exhaust\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Collect}} {{Small Card Infobox|Miracle}}\n{{C|Collect}} is an X {{Icon|PE}} cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives X (X+1 if upgraded) {{BD|Collect}}, which adds one upgraded {{C|Miracle}} to your hand at the start of every turn.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* {{BD|Collect}} takes effect before your cards are drawn. This means that it can cause you to draw less cards at the start of your turn due to the hand size limit.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{R|Chemical X}} makes {{C|Collect}} apply 2 more times, regardless of the amount of {{Icon|PE}} '''Energy''' used to play it.\n* If played through an effect such as {{P|Distilled Chaos}} or {{C|Omniscience}}, it will play for the full current {{Icon|PE}} '''Energy''' without actually using any.\n* Can be used with 0 {{Icon|PE}} '''Energy''' to advance {{R|Ink Bottle}} or {{R|Letter Opener}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* If {{C|Collect}} is duplicated with an effect such as a {{P|Duplication Potion}} or {{C|Burst}}, the value of X will also be used for the copy.\n* Being an X-cost, {{C|Collect}} can be {{C|Recycle|Recycled}} to double the current {{Icon|BE}} '''Energy'''.\n* It will not count as a 0-cost card for {{C|Scrape}} or {{C|All for One}}.\n* If a {{C|Miracle}} generated by this card exceeds your hand size limit, it gets added to the discard pile.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1959":{"pageid":1959,"ns":0,"title":"Deadly Poison","revisions":[{"revid":56781,"parentid":56040,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Deadly Poison\n|Image       = Green-DeadlyPoison.png\n|Color       = Green\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Apply (5;7) {{BD|Poison}}.\n|GivesToEnemy = Poison\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Poison}}{{C|Deadly Poison}} is a 1 {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\nAs {{BD|Poison}} applies at the start of the enemy's turn, it has some unusual interactions:\n* If the damage is enough to cause {{M|The Guardian}} to change to Defensive form, it will immediately change its [[Intent]] to apply {{BD|Sharp Hide}}. Moreover, as it is already past the point in its turn where {{KW|Block}} is removed, it will keep the Block generated by moving to Defensive Form until its next turn.\n** Notably, in other cases where HP thresholds affect enemy [[Intent]] (such as {{M|The Champ}} and {{M|Time Eater}}), this happens on a subsequent turn, and will not be affected.\n* If the enemy dies to {{BD|Poison}}, the card drawn by {{R|Gremlin Horn}} will be held until your next turn.\n** Similarly, if a {{M|Bronze Orb}} dies while holding a card in Stasis, that card will be returned to you and stay in your hand until next turn.\n* If a {{M|Fungi Beast}} dies this way, you will receive {{BD|Vulnerable}} during the enemy turn, which may increase the amount of incoming damage for the turn.\n* If an enemy with {{BD|Minion|Minions}} dies this way, its Minions will still flee combat before attacking.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{C|Bane}} does additional damage if the target has {{BD|Poison}}.\n* {{C|Catalyst}} can double (triple) the amount of {{BD|Poison}} on a target.\n* {{R|The Specimen}} can be used in combats with multiple enemies to consolidate {{BD|Poison}} as enemies die.\n* {{R|Snecko Skull}} applies 1 {{BD|Poison}} whenever this card applies {{BD|Poison}}.\n\n* {{C|Deadly Poison}} works well with other sources of {{BD|Poison}}:\n==== Cards ====\n* {{C|Poisoned Stab}}, {{C|Bouncing Flask}}, {{C|Crippling Cloud}}, {{C|Noxious Fumes}}, {{C|Corpse Explosion}}, {{C|Envenom}}.\n\n==== Relics and potions ====\n* {{R|Twisted Funnel}}.\n* {{P|Poison Potion}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* {{BD|Poison}} damage causes {{M|Lagavulin}} to wake up, consuming its Stunned turn in the process.\n* {{BD|Poison}} bypasses {{KW|Block}} and {{BD|Flying}}.\n* However, {{BD|Intangible}} reduces ''all'' sources of HP loss to 1, including {{BD|Poison}}.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* {{BD|Artifact}} will prevent applying {{BD|Poison}}.\n* Certain bosses will remove all [[Debuffs]] during combat: {{M|The Champ}}, {{M|Awakened One}}, and {{M|Time Eater}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 18: Paranormal'''\n** Deadly Poison card buff: 4 -> 5. Upgraded: 6 -> 7.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2279":{"pageid":2279,"ns":0,"title":"Empty Mind","revisions":[{"revid":54857,"parentid":50660,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Empty Mind\n|Image       = Purple-EmptyMind.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Exit your {{KW|Stance}}.<br>Draw (2;3) cards.\n|Keywords    = Draw\n}}\n{{C|Empty Mind}} is a 1 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It draws 2 (3 if upgraded) cards, and makes you exit your current {{KW|Stance}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* When you exit any {{KW|Stance}}, the following will occur:\n** Any {{C|Flurry of Blows}} that was in your discard pile will be brought back to your hand, as long as there is space in hand.\n** {{C|Mental Fortress}} will give {{KW|Block}}.\n** When you exit {{KW|Calm}}, it has the additional effect of giving you 2 {{Icon|PE}} '''Energy'''. This increases to 3 {{Icon|PE}} '''Energy''' if you have {{R|Violet Lotus}}.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1872":{"pageid":1872,"ns":0,"title":"Feed","revisions":[{"revid":56411,"parentid":56410,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Feed\n| Image       = Red-Feed.png\n| Color       = Red\n| Type        = Attack\n| Rarity      = Rare\n| Cost        = 1\n| Description = Deal (10;12) damage.<br>If {{KW|Fatal}}, raise your Max HP by (3;4). {{KW|Exhaust}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Exhaust\n| InteractsWith = Fatal\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Fatal}} {{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Feed}} is a 1 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 10 (12 if upgraded) damage, and if this damage is {{KW|Fatal}}, it will permanently increase your Max HP by 3 (4 if upgraded). {{C|Feed}} will then {{KW|Exhaust}} itself.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* As playing {{C|Feed}} at the right moment is crucial, it synergizes with {{R|Runic Pyramid}} and ways to {{KW|Retain}} it, such as {{C|Well-Laid Plans}}, {{C|Equilibrium}} or {{C|Meditate}}.\n\n* As one of the few cards that has benefits that remain outside of combat, triggering it as often as possible becomes an additional objective within combat. Given that {{C|Feed}} {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}} after use, it synergizes with:\n** {{R|Strange Spoon}}, which gives a 50% chance to not {{KW|Exhaust}} {{C|Feed}} when played, allowing it to be redrawn and used again.\n** {{C|Exhume}}, which can get {{C|Feed}} back once after being played, with the added benefit of putting it directly into your hand.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* When duplicated through an effect such as {{C|Double Tap}} or a {{P|Duplication Potion}}, {{C|Feed}} will trigger its {{KW|Fatal}} effect even if only the second play was {{KW|Fatal}}.\n** As duplicated {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attacks}} always target the same enemy with both plays, you cannot trigger {{C|Feed}} twice by duplicating it.\n\n* {{KW|Fatal}} does ''not'' trigger when {{BD|Minion|Minions}} are killed.\n** However, the {{M|Cultist}} enemies in {{M|Awakened One}} fight are not technically {{BD|Minion|Minions}}, and ''can'' trigger {{KW|Fatal}}.\n\n* {{KW|Fatal}} is not affected by {{M|Slime Boss}} or other Slime enemies splitting, and only triggers when reducing a Slime's health to 0, whether that Slime was spawned as the result of a split or not.\n* The first phase of {{M|Awakened One}} does not trigger {{KW|Fatal}}, but the second phase does.\n\n* In the {{M|Darkling|Three Darklings}} fight, an attack is only considered {{KW|Fatal}} if it kills the last {{M|Darkling}}; otherwise, unlimited triggers could be farmed on this fight.\n\n* {{KW|Fatal}} triggers on killing the {{M|Corrupt Heart}}, although this does not matter, as it ends the run.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* Due to the limited number of {{KW|Fatal}} triggers available in any given combat, {{C|Feed}} does not synergize with other {{KW|Fatal}} cards:\n* {{R|Mark of the Bloom}} prevents the healing from the Max HP increase. You will still gain Max HP.\n\n==== Cards ====\n* {{C|Hand of Greed}}\n* {{C|Ritual Dagger}}\n* {{C|Lesson Learned}}\n\n== Achievements ==\n=== Ooh Donut! ===\n* Unlocks when you kill {{M|Donu}} with Feed.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2104":{"pageid":2104,"ns":0,"title":"Glacier","revisions":[{"revid":55801,"parentid":50593,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Glacier\n|Image       = Blue-Glacier.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 2\n|Description = Gain (7;10) {{KW|Block}}.<br>{{KW|Channel}} 2 {{KW|Frost}}.\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Channel}} {{Keyword Infobox|Frost}}\n{{C|Glacier}} is a 2 {{Icon|BE}} cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}}. <!---It gains 7 (10) {{KW|Block}}, then {{KW|Channel|Channels}} 2 {{KW|Frost|Frost Orbs}}.--->\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n==== a) General Orb Synergies ====\n* Glacier works best with other Orb sources, such as {{C|Ball Lightning}} and {{C|Coolheaded}}, allowing Orbs to be {{KW|Evoke|Evoked}} more frequently. <!--- No idea what to include as prototypical orb gen cards, so just went with these two--->\n* {{C|Blizzard}} does more damage for each {{KW|Frost|Frost Orb}} {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} this combat.\n* Sources of {{BD|Focus}} will improve the effects of Orbs: {{C|Defragment}}, {{C|Consume}}, {{C|Biased Cognition}}, {{R|Data Disk}}\n* Sources of additional Orb Slots allow for having more [[Orbs#Passive|Orb Passives]] in parallel: {{C|Capacitor}}, {{R|Runic Capacitor}}, {{R|Inserter}}, {{P|Potion of Capacity}}\n* {{C|Compile Driver}} draws a card for each unique type of Orb {{KW|Channel|Channeled}}.\n* {{C|Barrage}} deals damage for each {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} Orb, while {{C|Fission}} draws a card and adds 1 {{Icon|BE}} for each Channeled Orb.\n* {{C|Recursion}}, {{C|Dualcast}}, and {{C|Multi-Cast}} each can directly {{KW|Evoke}} your Orbs 1, 2, or X times respectively.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* {{C|Reprogram}} and {{C|Hyperbeam}} give negative {{BD|Focus}}, making Orbs generated by Glacier less effective.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 37: Darkness'''\n** Glacier card nerf: 8 -> 7 Block. Glacier+ nerf: 11 -> 10 Block.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 34: Malaise'''\n** Glacier card nerf: Block 9 -> 8. Upgraded: 12 -> 11.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1802":{"pageid":1802,"ns":0,"title":"Grand Finale","revisions":[{"revid":55437,"parentid":50537,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Grand Finale\n|Image       = Green-GrandFinale.png\n|Color       = Green\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = Can only be played if there are no cards in your draw pile.<br>Deal (50;60) damage to ALL enemies.\n}}\n{{C|Grand Finale}} is a 0 {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 50 (60 if upgraded) damage to '''ALL''' enemies. It cannot be played if there are any cards in your draw pile.\n\n== Interactions == \n=== Synergies ===\n* {{R|Runic Pyramid}} or {{C|Well-Laid Plans}} can ensure the card is in hand when the draw pile approaches 0.\n** {{R|Runic Pyramid}}, and to a lesser degree {{KW|Retain}}, allow you to influence the amount of cards you draw at the start of the next turn, by leaving only that amount of space in hand when ending the current turn.\n\n* {{R|Wrist Blade}} increases the damage of this card by 4.\n\n* {{C|Grand Finale}} is difficult to play without sufficient draw control. A combination of fixed and variable draw cards, as well as some relics, can increase its playability:\n\n==== Cards ====\n* {{C|Acrobatics}}, {{C|Backflip}}, {{C|Dagger Throw}}, {{C|Prepared}}, {{C|Quick Slash}}, {{C|Escape Plan}}, {{C|Reflex}}, {{C|Adrenaline}}, {{C|Tools of the Trade}}, as well as any draw cards from other characters, most notably {{C|Scrape}}, which will draw 4 (5) cards, and will '''not''' [[Keywords#Discard|discard]] {{C|Grand Finale}} due to it being a 0-cost card.\n* {{C|Predator}} (fixed next-turn draw)\n* {{C|Doppelganger}} (variable next-turn draw)\n* {{C|Calculated Gamble}} (variable draw)\n* {{C|Expertise}} (variable draw)\n\n==== Relics ====\n* {{R|Gambling Chip}} is a source of variable draw. \n* {{R|Ink Bottle}} may affect draw.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V1.1: The Dealer'''\n** Grand Finale card is now 0.3s faster in Fast Mode.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 46: Adrenaline'''\n** Grand Finale card buff: 40 -> 50 damage. Grand Finale+: 50 -> 60 damage.\n** Adding VFX for Grand Finale card.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 19: Seed'''\n** Grand Finale card buff. Cost 1 -> 0.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 2: Slimes!'''\n** Grand Finale now costs 1 (was 2).\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1879":{"pageid":1879,"ns":0,"title":"Immolate","revisions":[{"revid":50462,"parentid":35988,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Immolate\n|Image       = Red-Immolate.png\n|Color       = Red\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = 2\n|Description = Deal (21;28) damage to ALL enemies.<br>Add a {{C|Burn}} into your discard pile.\n}}\n{{Small Card Infobox|Burn}}{{C|Immolate}} is a 2 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 21 (28 if upgraded) to '''ALL''' enemies and adds a {{C|Burn}} into your discard pile.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order === \n* The {{C|Burn}} gets added into your discard pile ''before'' triggering {{R|Ink Bottle}}, meaning it can be drawn if your draw pile is empty.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* Synergizes with {{C|Fire Breathing}} and {{C|Evolve}}, as it creates a {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Status|Status}} card in your discard pile. However, as it gets created in your discard pile, it can take some time before it can be drawn to trigger these effects.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* Hexaghost can upgrade all {{C|Burn|Burns}} in the draw and discard pile, meaning it will also upgrade {{C|Burn|Burns}} generated by this card.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 21: Channel Lightning'''\n** Immolate card buff: Adds a Burn to discard pile instead of draw pile.\n** Immolate card buff: 18 -> 21 damage.\n** Immolate+ card buff: 24 -> 28 damage.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 20: Immolate'''\n** Immolate now costs 2, deals considerably more damage, and shuffles a Burn into your draw pile.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 3: Balance Balance Balance'''\n** Immolate now uses proper exhausting. Triggers stuff better and Purity Achievement works with it.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2207":{"pageid":2207,"ns":0,"title":"Machine Learning","revisions":[{"revid":55845,"parentid":50623,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Machine Learning\n|Image       = Blue-MachineLearning.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Power\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = (;{{KW|Innate}}. <br>)At the start of your turn, draw 1 additional card.\n|Keywords    = Draw\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Draw}}{{C|Machine Learning}} is a 1 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} Card. It gives 1 {{BD|Draw}}, which increases the amount of cards you draw at the start of your turn. When upgraded, it becomes {{KW|Innate}}, meaning it will always appear in your first hand of combat.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2395":{"pageid":2395,"ns":0,"title":"Omega","revisions":[{"revid":53188,"parentid":50761,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"#REDIRECT [[Alpha#Omega]]"}}}]},"1954":{"pageid":1954,"ns":0,"title":"Regret","revisions":[{"revid":56778,"parentid":55920,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Regret\n|Image       = Curse-Regret.png\n|Color       = Colorless\n|Type        = Curse\n|Cost        = -2\n|NoUpgrade   = true\n|Description = {{KW|Unplayable}}.<br>At the end of your turn, lose HP equal to the number of cards in your hand.\n|GivesToPlayer = Unplayable\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Unplayable}}\n{{C|Regret}} is an {{KW|Unplayable}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}} Card. If it is in your hand at end of turn, it will cause you to lose HP equal to the amount of cards still in your hand. This counts the number of cards in your hand at the time you press the End Turn button, and so includes Regret itself. \nThis card will also forcibly [[Keywords#Discard|discard]] itself at the end of its turn, even if you {{KW|Retain}} it or have {{R|Runic Pyramid}}.\n\n== Obtaining Decay ==\nLike most {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curses}}, Regret can be obtained from anything that gives a random Curse:\n* Can be part of Neow's [[Third Blessing]] in exchange for a reward.\n* {{E|Match and Keep}}.\n* {{R|Cursed Key}}.\n* {{KW|Transform|Transforming}} another Curse.\n\nIn addition, Regret can be obtained from both the {{E|Big Fish}} Event when choosing the {{Frame|Box}} and {{E|Golden Shrine}} when choosing {{Frame|Desecrate}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* Regret will discard itself at the end of your turn before the rest of your hand, at the same time it applies the HP loss. This happens ''before'' {{KW|Retain}} happens, so you cannot choose to Retain it.\n<!--- I'm just including the main extra interactions here, but with the ones not relevant to the current page commented away. This allows easy transfer to related pages.--->\n* '''Regret''', {{C|Decay}}, {{C|Burn|Burns}}, {{C|Shame}}, and {{C|Doubt}} all activate at the same time at end of turn. Visually they activate from left to right. However:\n** Regardless of the order of activation, Regret counts any copies of the others as being still in your hand when its damage is applied.\n*** Regret does ''not'' take into account cards drawn from {{R|Runic Cube}} as a result of taking damage from these cards; it will always just use the number of cards in your hand when your turn ended.\n** If Regret, {{C|Decay}}, or {{C|Burn}} cause you to draw into any of the above via {{R|Runic Cube}}, those newly drawn cards will ''not'' go off, and will be discarded with the rest of your hand.\n** The damage for Regret, {{C|Burn}}, and {{C|Decay}} are applied from left to right. So, if you have 1 stack of {{BD|Buffer}} and two of them in hand, the left one will have its damage consumed, and the right one will apply.\n*** When selecting cards from your hand, such as to [[Keywords#Discard|discard]] or {{KW|Exhaust}}, you can freely reorder your hand, as selecting and then unselecting a card moves it to the last spot in your hand. If needed, this can be used to manipulate which card's damage is applied to you.\n<!---** For Shame and {{C|Doubt}}, the {{KW|Debuff|Debuffs}} are applied from left to right. So, if you have 1 stack of {{BD|Artifact}} and both in hand, the left one will consume the Artifact and the right one will apply.\n*** When selecting cards from your hand, such as to [[Keywords#Discard|discard]] or {{KW|Exhaust}}, you can freely reorder your hand, as selecting and then unselecting a card moves it to the last spot in your hand. If needed, this can be used to manipulate which Curse's debuff is applied to you.--->\n\n=== Synergies ===\nAs Regret is a '''{{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}}''', it interacts with the following:\n* {{C|Fire Breathing}} will deal damage when it is drawn.\n* {{R|Du-Vu Doll}} will give you 1 {{BD|Strength}} each combat.\n* {{R|Blue Candle}} can be used to {{KW|Exhaust}} it for 1 HP. \n* When added to the deck, it will be negated by {{R|Omamori}}, or gain you 6 max HP if you have {{R|Darkstone Periapt}} and ''not'' Omamori.\n\nThe HP loss from Regret can be:\n* Negated with {{BD|Buffer}}, via {{R|Fossilized Helix}} and {{C|Buffer}}.\n* Reduced to 1 with {{BD|Intangible}}, via {{R|Incense Burner}}, {{C|Wraith Form}}, and {{C|Apparition}}.\n* Reduced by 1 with {{R|Tungsten Rod}}.\n\nThe HP loss from Regret can also be used to your benefit:\n* Losing HP causes {{R|Runic Cube}} to draw you a card.\n* {{C|Blood for Blood}} will have its cost reduced for the rest of combat.\n* The HP loss is counted as being from a card, so {{C|Rupture}} will gain you {{BD|Strength}}.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* As {{C|Clash}} can only be played when all cards in your hand are {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attacks}}, if it is drawn at the same time as Regret, it cannot be played.\n* Losing HP from Regret causes {{C|Masterful Stab}} will have its cost increased for the rest of combat.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* As most Curses are only given in a single Event (not counting random ones), Regret is tied with {{C|Writhe}} and {{C|Parasite}} for being the Curse with the most ways to get it.\n* This card's [[Beta Art]] references the fact that {{M|Byrd|Byrds}} become significantly more dangerous with {{BD|Strength}} due to its {{Int|Byrd|Peck}} move. {{R|Philosopher's Stone}} gives enemies 1 {{BD|Strength}}, which doubles {{M|Byrd|Byrds'}} damage output.\n\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2451":{"pageid":2451,"ns":0,"title":"Safety","revisions":[{"revid":53289,"parentid":50763,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"#REDIRECT [[Deceive Reality#Safety]]"}}}]},"1850":{"pageid":1850,"ns":0,"title":"Second Wind","revisions":[{"revid":56400,"parentid":55933,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Second Wind\n| Image       = Red-SecondWind.png\n| Color       = Red\n| Type        = Skill\n| Rarity      = Uncommon\n| Cost        = 1\n| Description = {{KW|Exhaust}} all non-Attack cards in your hand. Gain (5;7) {{KW|Block}} for each card {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Exhaust, Block\n| InteractsWith = Exhaust\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}} {{Keyword Infobox|Block}}\n{{C|Second Wind}} is a 1 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}} all non-{{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} cards in your hand, and you gain 5 (7 if upgraded) {{KW|Block}} for every card {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}} this way.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* {{C|Second Wind}} will already be removed from hand when {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausting}} all non-{{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} cards in your hand, meaning it will not {{KW|Exhaust}} itself.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{C|Second Wind}} has {{KW|Exhaust}}-synergy with {{C|Dark Embrace}}, {{C|Feel No Pain}}, {{R|Charon's Ashes}} and {{R|Dead Branch}}, and can reliably {{KW|Exhaust}} {{C|Sentinel}}.\n* Second Wind can be used to get rid of unwanted cards in hand, such as {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Status|Status}} or {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}} cards.\n* Each card {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}} counts as a separate instance of gaining {{KW|Block}}, meaning it scales well with {{BD|Dexterity}} and can trigger {{C|Juggernaut}} multiple times.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V1.1: The Dealer'''\n** Fixed Second Wind doing its effects in reverse and only gaining one instance of block.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1841":{"pageid":1841,"ns":0,"title":"Shrug It Off","revisions":[{"revid":56393,"parentid":50402,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Shrug It Off\n| Image       = Red-ShrugItOff.png\n| Color       = Red\n| Type        = Skill\n| Rarity      = Common\n| Cost        = 1\n| Description = Gain (8;11) {{KW|Block}}.<br>Draw 1 card.\n| GivesToPlayer = Block, Draw\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Block}}\n{{C|Shrug It Off}} is a 1 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 8 (11 if upgraded) {{KW|Block}} and draws 1 card.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2420":{"pageid":2420,"ns":0,"title":"Signature Move","revisions":[{"revid":55940,"parentid":50680,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Signature Move\n|Image       = Purple-SignatureMove.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 2\n|Description = Can only be played if this is the only Attack in your hand. <br>Deal (30;40) damage.\n|Keywords    = Hand\n}}\n{{C|Signature Move}} is a 2 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 30 (40 if upgraded) damage. It cannot be played if any other card in hand is an {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* Synergizes well with hand-management through for example {{KW|Exhaust}} or [[Keywords#Discard|discard]] effects.\n* When drawing it through {{R|Unceasing Top}}, the only card in hand will be {{C|Signature Move}}, meaning it can be played.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* If the condition is not met, {{C|Signature Move}} will simply not be able to be played. This includes if it is played through for example {{P|Distilled Chaos}} or {{C|Omniscience}}. These will cause {{C|Signature Move}} to simply discard itself without being played, unless {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}}. This means:\n** [[Time Eater]]'s {{BD|Time Warp}} is not triggered.\n** {{R|Ink Bottle}} is not advanced.\n** {{R|Nunchaku}}, {{R|Kunai}}, {{R|Shuriken}} and {{R|Ornamental Fan}} are not triggered.\n\n* While {{C|Omniscience}} will not play an unplayable {{C|Signature Move}}, it will still {{KW|Exhaust}} it.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* As opposed to most cards and strategies in this game, this card pairs poorly with effects that allow you to draw cards, except for previously mentioned {{R|Unceasing Top}}. \n* It pairs poorly with {{R|Dead Branch}}, since {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausting}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} cards is a way to enable you to play {{C|Signature Move}}, but this can possibly replace those cards with other {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} cards.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1436":{"pageid":1436,"ns":0,"title":"Strike (Silent)","revisions":[{"revid":50469,"parentid":43164,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}} \n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Strike (Silent)\n|DisplayName = Strike\n|Image       = Green-Strike.png\n|Color       = Green\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Basic\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Deal (6;9) damage.\n}}\n{{C|Strike (Silent)|Strike}} is a 1 {{Icon|GE}} cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Basic|Basic}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 6 (9 if upgraded) damage.\n\nThis page is for Silent's version of Strike. Go here for {{C|Strike (Ironclad)}}, {{C|Strike (Defect)}}, {{C|Strike (Watcher)}}.\n\n== Obtaining Strike ==\nThe [[Silent]] starts with 5 copies of {{C|Strike (Silent)|Strike}} in her deck. It cannot be obtained through regular card rewards.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{C|Strike (Silent)|Strike}} gets a damage increase of 3 from {{R|Strike Dummy}}, and adds to the damage of {{C|Perfected Strike}}.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* The beta art version of strike is based off the Batman slapping Robin meme.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V1.1: The Dealer'''\n** Silent's starting Strikes are put before Defends (to be consistent with other characters)\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 18: Paranormal'''\n** Perfected Strike now counts Strikes from other characters.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 1: The First of Many!'''\n** Falling Event can now hit Strikes and Defends, making the event potentially not as bad.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2116":{"pageid":2116,"ns":0,"title":"Thunder Strike","revisions":[{"revid":55978,"parentid":50629,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Thunder Strike\n|Image       = Blue-ThunderStrike.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = 3\n|Description = Deal (7;9) damage to a random enemy for each {{KW|Lightning}} {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} this combat.\n}} \n{{Keyword Infobox|Lightning}} {{Keyword Infobox|Channel}}\n{{C|Thunder Strike}} is a 3 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. <!--It does 7 (10) damage to a random enemy for each {{KW|Lightning|Lightning Orb}} {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} this combat.-->\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* Thunder Strike benefits from all sources of {{KW|Lightning|Lightning Orbs}}, especially {{C|Tempest}}, {{C|Static Discharge}}, and {{C|Electrodynamics}}, which can {{KW|Channel}} multiple at once.\n\n* {{C|Thunder Strike}} gets a damage increase of 3 for every hit from {{R|Strike Dummy}}, and adds to the damage of {{C|Perfected Strike}}.\n\n* Benefits once from {{BD|Strength}} or {{BD|Vigor}} per hit, so for every {{KW|Lightning}} {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} before this card is played.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* Despite the similarity to the random targeting of {{KW|Lightning|Lightning Orbs}}, Thunder Strike is unaffected by {{BD|Electro}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V1.1: The Dealer'''\n** Fixed Rip and Tear, Sword Boomerang, and Thunder Strike continuing its hits over Thorns and Shifting powers.\n** Fixed Wrist Blade not affecting Sword Boomerang, Rip and Tear, and Thunder Strike.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 54: Loop'''\n** Tingsha, Sword Boomerang, Bouncing Flask, Rip and Tear, Thunder Orbs, Havoc, and Juggernaut now utilize seeded enemy target randomization.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 37: Darkness'''\n** Thunderstrike card no longer shoots a single lightning if you have channeled no Lightning.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 28: The Ritual'''\n** Fixed issue where Strike (blue), Thunder Strike, and Meteor Strike weren't used by Perfected Strike.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1868":{"pageid":1868,"ns":0,"title":"True Grit","revisions":[{"revid":56408,"parentid":50405,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = True Grit\n| Image       = Red-TrueGrit.png\n| Color       = Red\n| Type        = Skill\n| Rarity      = Common\n| Cost        = 1\n| Description = Gain (7;9) {{KW|Block}}.<br>{{KW|Exhaust}} 1 card( at random;).\n| GivesToPlayer = Exhaust, Block\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Block}} {{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|True Grit}} is a 1 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 7 {{KW|Block}} and randomly {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}} one card in your hand. If it is upgraded, it allows you to select one card in hand to {{KW|Exhaust}} instead. If there are no other cards in hand when this card is played, no card will be {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{C|True Grit}} has {{KW|Exhaust}}-synergy with {{C|Dark Embrace}}, {{C|Feel No Pain}}, {{R|Charon's Ashes}}, and {{R|Dead Branch}}, and, if upgraded, can reliably {{KW|Exhaust}} {{C|Sentinel}}.\n* Upgraded {{C|True Grit}} can be used to get rid of unwanted cards in hand, such as {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Status|Status}} or {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}} cards.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 47: Metamorphosis'''\n** Fixed issue where True Grit card was not behaving correctly with seeded runs.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 23: Testing Continues...'''\n** True Grit card is now properly seeded.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]}}}}